{title: Brother To Brother}
{artist: Larry Holder / Elton Smith}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 80}

>Lyrics

(Short introduction)

Verse 1

Thank you, my brother,

for being around,

For stopping to listen

when I was cast down.

For being a brother

and lending a hand,

For prayers that you offered

that helped me to stand.

Refrain

Brother to brother

is how we must live

There are times we receive,

just as times we're to give.

The care and compassion

are stars in your crown

For being my brother

when I was cast down.

Verse 2

So take heart, my brother

if ever you're down.

I'll stand right beside you

and always be found.

And when we've departed,

though time is like sand,

We'll rejoice up in heaven,

as brother and friend.

(Repeat Refrain)

Brother to brother

is how we must live

There are times we receive,

just as times we're to give.

The care and compassion

are stars in your crown

For being my brother

when I was cast down.
